<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Baldwin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1804">1804</a>–<a href="/years/1858">1858</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Baldwin was a lawyer and Reform politician of Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and Canada West, the leading advocate of responsible government. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-hippolyte-lafontaine">Louis-Hippolyte LaFontaine</a> he led the ministry of 1848 to 1851, which established that the cabinet must keep the confidence of the elected assembly. His government also reformed municipal institutions and turned King's College into the secular University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-baldwin.jpg" alt="Robert Baldwin" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miscellaneous Collection/Library and Archives Canada/C-031493 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RobertBaldwin23.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
